    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear objective: capitalize on favorable velocity matchups to bolster our stolen base totals. The anchor of our lineup is **Corbin Carroll** (85.07), who finds himself in an ideal spot against Zack Littell. While Littell\u2019s ability to hold runners mitigates the SB ceiling slightly, the +19% SP skill boost and a +6% platoon advantage project a massive day for **Corbin Carroll** at the #3 spot. He is joined in the elite tier by **Josh Naylor** (77.76), who benefits from a generous wind-out forecast and a favorable matchup against Keider Montero, and **James Wood** (73.03), whose elite 0.401 xwOBA against left-handed pitcher Eduardo Rodriguez makes him a high-floor start despite the neutral platoon dynamic. **Gabriel Moreno** (71.16) and **Brice Turang** (67.77) round out the top tier, with **Brice Turang** receiving a significant +14% boost from park factors that keep his efficiency high.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Austin Riley** (44.31), who fell just shy of the threshold for a start. Despite his pedigree, the +19% SP skill of Braxton Ashcraft\u2014combined with a restrictive #7 spot in the order\u2014pushed **Austin Riley** into the marginal category. We have opted to prioritize the dynamic platoon edge of **Jose Caballero** (67.57) and the raw opportunity of **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.05), both of whom offer more immediate upside against their respective right-handed opponents. While **Zach McKinstry** (43.95) and **Kyle Karros** (39.26) remain on the bench, they serve as our primary depth should any of the projected lineups shift negatively before first pitch.\n\nManagers should remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, as our scoring relies heavily on the assumed batting order positions. The primary risk today involves **Dalton Rushing** (56.17) and **Alex Freeland** (52.18); both are currently hovering in the marginal zone due to bottom-of-the-order placement. If the official lineups move **Dalton Rushing** or **Alex Freeland** up, we could see a rapid spike in efficiency. Additionally, while we are tracking **Mickey Moniak** on the IL, the rest of the roster remains healthy and ready to ride the whip. Keep a close eye on the wind reports in the **Josh Naylor** and **Jose Caballero** games, as any shift in direction could impact the viability of our power-dependent hitters.",
